8. What I Learned

This project helped me understand how a Python application can be separated into different files instead of putting everything into one large program.

I learned that:

* `models.py` defines the objects and their behaviour.
* `storage.py` handles saving and loading information.
* `task_manager.py` contains the main application logic.
* `cli.py` handles user commands.
* `test_task_manager.py` checks whether the functionality works correctly.
