9. My Reflection

At the beginning, I did not fully understand how all the files connected to each other. I mainly focused on getting the program to run, but while fixing the errors I started understanding what each file was responsible for.

The biggest thing I learned was that fixing code is not only about changing lines until the error disappears. I need to understand why the error happened and how the different parts of the project are supposed to work together.

I also learned the importance of testing after making changes. Getting `python cli.py` to display the help menu showed that the CLI could start, but running the unit tests is what will give me more confidence that the individual functions are working correctly.

